From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emulationstation: GAMEPAD PROFILE selector (Xbox Elite / DualSense)

Add a "GAMEPAD PROFILE" selector under Main Menu > System Settings >
PERFORMANCE and in the Quick Access modal, next to the CHARGING MODE selector:

  XBOX ELITE (PADDLES) / DUALSENSE EDGE (PADDLES)

Xbox Elite is the only InputPlumber target whose emulated pad exposes the AYN
Odin 3 back paddles as evdev buttons (-> game buttons P1/P3 and the left-home
capture combo); DualSense is a plain PlayStation pad, no paddles. Persists inputplumber.profile and
drives /usr/bin/gamepad-profile, which swaps the InputPlumber target and (for
ds5) strips the paddle-source so input_sense still reads raw KEY_F13/F14 for
capture. Gated on the Odin 3 InputPlumber composite, so it is hidden elsewhere.

Applies after patch 011 (charge-mode): it inserts right after the CHARGING MODE
blocks that patch introduces, so it must apply in numeric filename order.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
 es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
@@ -2012,6 +2012,27 @@
 		});
 	}
 
+	// Gamepad profile: Xbox Elite (the AYN Odin 3 back paddles work as real game
+	// buttons P1/P3) vs DualSense (PlayStation layout, no paddles). Only on the Odin 3,
+	// which ships this InputPlumber composite. Driven by /usr/bin/gamepad-profile;
+	// the screen-capture combo works in either profile.
+	if (Utils::FileSystem::exists("/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/01-ayn-controller.yaml")) {
+		auto gamepad_profile = std::make_shared<OptionListComponent<std::string> >(mWindow, _("GAMEPAD PROFILE"), false);
+		std::string curGamepadProfile = SystemConf::getInstance()->get("inputplumber.profile");
+		if (curGamepadProfile.empty() || curGamepadProfile == "xbox-series")
+			curGamepadProfile = "xbox-elite";
+		else if (curGamepadProfile == "ds5-edge")
+			curGamepadProfile = "ds5";
+		gamepad_profile->add(_("XBOX ELITE (PADDLES)"), "xbox-elite", curGamepadProfile == "xbox-elite");
+		gamepad_profile->add(_("DUALSENSE EDGE (PADDLES)"), "ds5", curGamepadProfile == "ds5");
+		s->addWithLabel(_("GAMEPAD PROFILE"), gamepad_profile);
+		gamepad_profile->setSelectedChangedCallback([](const std::string& prof) {
+			SystemConf::getInstance()->set("inputplumber.profile", prof);
+			SystemConf::getInstance()->saveSystemConf();
+			Utils::Platform::runSystemCommand("/usr/bin/gamepad-profile set " + prof, "", nullptr);
+		});
+	}
+
